From 00c6172e38259a0fdeb001c91920df9001a15826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grafici patch export <patch-export@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:40:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Make examples portable to AVR C++11 and document the checked
 contracts

Replace C++17 class template argument deduction in the area example with
DataArrayXY<float>. Animation resolution is an integer sample count, and its
callback accesses the global offset without an invalid lambda capture.
Remove redundant function-definition semicolons rejected in strict checks
by older AVR compilers. These changes add no runtime buffer or allocation.

Add a Python runner for all ten strict C++11 regressions and two expected
compile-time template rejections. Document boundary semantics and update
the matched float/FP16 flash/SRAM measurements after the correctness fixes.

Validation: all host checks pass with UBSan and float-cast-overflow. All eight
examples compile with AVR GCC 7.3.0 in GNU C++11, also without -fpermissive and
with narrowing errors enabled. Six link within Uno R3 flash; area and the
scatter/histogram example exceed it. Static sizes exclude heap/stack peaks;
see patches/correctness/README.md for the per-example audit.
